# Verdict Capture — the shared store (T2)

## The goal

Make things repeated less. Every accept/reject/correct is a verdict — a
structural fact about what the AI did right or wrong. T2 records verdicts
into the shared store automatically and injects recent ones back into the
session so the AI cannot re-walk a rejected path.

## The shared store

One SQLite database is the single source of truth for manage state:

- Per-project: `<project>/.opencode/state.db`
- Global: `~/.config/opencode/state.db` (cross-project structures)

The AI never writes to it — the airlock denies all mutation tools; the AI's
only channels are emit_proposal / registry_propose. Writers: the nvim
viewer (user actions → verdicts). Readers: the plugin (injection), the
sidecar (T4, metrics). One store, one manager, no JSONL sprawl.

## Schema v1 — verdicts

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS verdicts (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  ts INTEGER NOT NULL,              -- ms epoch
  session_id TEXT,
  proposal_id INTEGER,              -- null for interrupt corrections
  group_name TEXT,
  path TEXT NOT NULL,
  operation TEXT,                   -- create|replace|edit_range|delete
  verdict TEXT NOT NULL,            -- accepted|rejected|corrected|moved_old
  reason TEXT,
  proposed_content TEXT,            -- what the AI proposed
  applied_content TEXT,             -- what was actually applied (null on reject)
  project TEXT,                     -- project slug
  scope TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'project'  -- project|global
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_verdicts_path ON verdicts(path);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_verdicts_ts ON verdicts(ts);
```

The correction is recoverable: proposed vs applied content IS the diff —
lossless, zero compute at capture. Consumers diff on read.

## Capture points (nvim)

| Action | Verdict | Recorded |
|---|---|---|
| `da` unchanged | accepted | proposed == applied |
| `da` after editing | corrected | proposed != applied — the diff is the structural fact |
| `dr` | rejected | applied_content null |
| delete confirm | moved_old | applied_content null |

## Global promotion

Same path + verdict seen in ≥2 distinct projects → also written to the
global store (scope='global'). Global verdicts inject everywhere.

## Injection (plugin)

`experimental.chat.messages.transform` appends the last ~5 verdicts for the
project (plus global) to the next call, compact:

```
[verdicts] Rejected: src/foo.ts (wrong interpretation) · Corrected: src/bar.go (2 hunks)
```

Loop-breaking only. No pruning, no evaluation, no demotion — those are T4/T5.

## Non-goals (this milestone)

- No pruning / context removal (T4)
- No evaluation / credit assignment (T5)
- No migration of proposals/journal/registry into state.db — additive only;
  they migrate as later milestones touch them

## Drivers

- nvim: sqlite.lua (FFI) or vim-dadbod
- plugin: node:sqlite (built-in) or better-sqlite3 fallback
- sidecar (T4): same file, new tables
